1471 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 907 0 R
/E (They sign up for every platform without tracking results. Running 4 platforms simultaneously means no route density, more deadhead miles, and constant context-switching. One focused lane with repeat stops almost always outearns scattered multi-platform work.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1472 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 907 0 R
/E (They skip insurance. Commercial auto insurance costs $150-$300/month depending on vehicle and coverage. Without it, one accident on a delivery run can end your business and leave you personally liable for $50,000+.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1473 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 907 0 R
/E (They buy vehicles before securing work. A $35,000 cargo van with no contracts is a $600/month payment draining savings. Prove demand with your current vehicle first, then upgrade when revenue justifies the cost.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1474 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 907 0 R
/E (They avoid direct outreach. Cold-calling 10 local businesses per week is uncomfortable but effective. One $180/day contract replaces the need to refresh a platform screen 50 times hoping for a decent route.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
