2268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 921 0 R
/E (SOLE PROPRIETOR VS LLC)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 921 0 R
/E (25)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 921 0 R
/E (Sole proprietor: zero paperwork to start. You earn money, you report it on Schedule C. Cost: $0. Downside: your personal assets \(car, savings, home equity\) are exposed if someone sues you for a delivery accident. One $50K lawsuit can wipe you out.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 921 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
2272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 921 0 R
/E (An LLC means nothing if you mix personal and business money. Courts call this piercing the corporate veil. If you pay rent from your business account or deposit business income into personal checking, the LLC protection disappears.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
2273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 921 0 R
/E (Open a free business checking account \(Relay, Novo, or a local credit union\). All delivery income deposits here. All business expenses paid from here. Transfer yourself a fixed weekly paycheck to personal. This creates a clean paper trail for taxes and liability protection.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
2274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 921 0 R
/E (Timeline: Start as sole proprietor for weeks 1-12 while proving income. Once you confirm $800+/week consistently, file your LLC and open the business account. Do not spend $500 on an LLC before you have earned $500 in delivery income. Prove the model first.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
